# Element Capture Extension - Implementation Tasks

Goal: Create the best "copy element" Chrome extension with minimal CSS/HTML output.

================================================================================
PHASE 0: Competitor Analysis & Research
================================================================================

## DivMagic Analysis
- [ ] Review DivMagic manifest.json and extension architecture
- [ ] Extract CSS property whitelist from blockRegistration.bundle.js (documented in DIVMAGIC_EXTRACT_COPY_ELEMENT_PROCESS.md)
- [ ] Document DivMagic's 3 copy modes: Adaptable, Balanced, Exact
- [ ] Analyze how DivMagic handles pseudo-elements in Balanced/Exact modes
- [ ] Document DivMagic's style output formats: Inline CSS, External CSS, Local CSS
- [ ] Extract DivMagic's media query handling approach
- [ ] Document DivMagic's WordPress block mapping strategy
- [ ] Note DivMagic's htmlparser2 and html-to-react usage for output formatting

## SnipCSS Analysis
- [ ] Review SnipCSS manifest.json and extension architecture
- [ ] Analyze contentscript_kiwi.js for element labeling strategy (snipcss classes)
- [ ] Document snipbackground.js CSS extraction pipeline
- [ ] Extract SnipCSS's selector fixing algorithm (snipcssFixSelector)
- [ ] Document inherited rule handling approach
- [ ] Analyze CSS variable resolution logic
- [ ] Document media query parsing and grouping approach
- [ ] Review "transmogrify" feature for class renaming/scoping
- [ ] Document multi-element selection workflow
- [ ] Analyze subselection (include/exclude) feature
- [ ] Review Tailwind conversion approach (v1.9.0+)

## Comparison & Best Practices Document
- [ ] Create comparison table: DivMagic vs SnipCSS feature parity
- [ ] Identify CSS properties both tools extract (common whitelist)
- [ ] Document properties SnipCSS extracts that DivMagic doesn't (and vice versa)
- [ ] Identify style minimization techniques from both tools
- [ ] Document selector specificity handling differences
- [ ] List edge cases each tool handles (or fails on)
- [ ] Define our target CSS property whitelist for minimal output

================================================================================
PHASE 1: Element Selection & DOM Capture
================================================================================

## Element Selection UI
- [ ] Implement element picker activation from popup
- [ ] Create hover highlight overlay (2px solid #3b82f6 border, rgba(59,130,246,0.08) bg)
- [ ] Implement tooltip showing tag name + dimensions
- [ ] Add click handler for element selection
- [ ] Implement parent traversal controls (expand selection)
- [ ] Handle overlay/fixed elements blocking selection (SnipCSS workaround)
- [ ] Prevent selection of SnipCSS/extension UI elements

## DOM Cloning
- [ ] Implement cloneNode(true) for subtree
- [ ] Remove script tags from clone
- [ ] Remove inline event handlers (onclick, onmouseover, onload)
- [ ] Remove tracking/analytics attributes (data-testid, data-reactroot, ng-*)
- [ ] Preserve essential attributes (src, href, alt, title, aria-*)
- [ ] Handle Shadow DOM detection and warning

================================================================================
PHASE 2: Style Extraction (Minimal Output Focus)
================================================================================

## Computed Style Extraction
- [ ] Implement getComputedStyle extraction for all nodes
- [ ] Create element traversal with parent-child tracking
- [ ] Handle text nodes separately from element nodes

## CSS Property Filtering (Core - Minimal Set)
- [ ] Define minimal property whitelist from competitor analysis
- [ ] Implement default value detection and omission
- [ ] Filter layout properties: display, position, top/right/bottom/left
- [ ] Filter box model: width, height, margin, padding, border, box-sizing
- [ ] Filter flex/grid: flex-*, justify-content, align-items, gap, grid-*
- [ ] Filter typography: font-*, line-height, letter-spacing, text-*
- [ ] Filter colors: color, background, background-color, background-image
- [ ] Filter visual: opacity, border-radius, box-shadow
- [ ] Omit inherited defaults (position: static, margin: 0, opacity: 1)

## CSS Variable Resolution
- [ ] Detect var(--*) in computed values
- [ ] Resolve variables to computed RGB/hex values
- [ ] Handle nested/recursive CSS variables (SnipCSS v1.7.0)
- [ ] Preserve CSS variables option (advanced feature)

================================================================================
PHASE 3: Pseudo Elements & Special Cases
================================================================================

## Pseudo Element Handling
- [ ] Detect ::before content via getComputedStyle(el, "::before")
- [ ] Detect ::after content via getComputedStyle(el, "::after")
- [ ] Convert pseudo elements to real elements with inline styles
- [ ] Handle pseudo element positioning (absolute, etc.)

## Image Handling
- [ ] Detect <img> tags and preserve src/alt
- [ ] Convert relative URLs to absolute URLs
- [ ] Preserve srcset or simplify to single src (SnipCSS approach)
- [ ] Option: Replace images with placeholder divs

## Background Image Handling
- [ ] Detect background-image in computed styles
- [ ] Extract and absolutize URLs
- [ ] Handle gradient backgrounds

## SVG Handling
- [ ] Preserve inline SVG markup and attributes
- [ ] Preserve viewBox attribute
- [ ] Use createElementNS for SVG cloning
- [ ] Handle SVG sprite references (<use href="...">)

