================================================================================
NOTES
================================================================================

Key insights from competitor analysis:
- DivMagic uses a CSS property whitelist for cleaner output
- SnipCSS uses Chrome debugger for advanced CSS rule extraction
- Both struggle with inherited styles and selector specificity
- CSS variable resolution is critical for modern sites
- Minimal output = remove defaults + use shorthands + remove inherited

Our differentiation:
- Minimal CSS output (smallest possible while preserving appearance)
- Clean, readable code (no framework artifacts)
- MCP integration for AI workflows
- Snippet library for reuse
